#+TITLE: ucspi-ssl — DSMR Package Documentation
#+AUTHOR: Brian O'Reilly <fade@deepsky.com>
#+DATE: 2026-03-22

* Summary

~ucspi-ssl~ packages the fehcom.de fork of ucspi-ssl (0.13.07) by Erwin
Hoffman.  It provides ~sslserver~ and ~sslclient~ — UCSPI-compatible TCP
wrappers that layer TLS/SSL onto stdin/stdout for djbware services such as
qmail SMTP and IMAP.  Supports OpenSSL 3.x and TLS 1.3.

| Field       | Value                              |
|-------------+------------------------------------|
| Source      | ucspi-ssl                          |
| Binary      | ucspi-ssl                          |
| Version     | 0.13.07-1                          |
| Architecture| any                                |
| Binaries in | ~/usr/bin/~                        |
| Build-dep   | fehqlibs-dev, libssl-dev           |
| Target      | Debian 13 Trixie                   |

* Description

The UCSPI (Unix Client-Server Program Interface) convention separates network
programs from their transport: a server program reads from fd 0 and writes to
fd 6; the UCSPI server wrapper handles bind, accept, and (with ucspi-ssl)
TLS negotiation before execing the application.

ucspi-ssl provides:

- ~sslserver~ — a TLS-capable tcpserver replacement; accepts connections,
  performs TLS handshake, and execs a child program.
- ~sslclient~ — connects to a TLS server and wires it to stdin/stdout of a
  child program.
- ~sslio~ — glues a plaintext UCSPI server to a TLS session, enabling STARTTLS
  without the inner server knowing about TLS.
- Supporting tools: ~sslprint~, ~sslcat~, ~certcheck~, ~who@~, and others.

In the DSMR stack ucspi-ssl is used by the ~qmail-submission~ supervise script
to wrap SMTP submission (port 587) with TLS.

** Relationship to fehqlibs

ucspi-ssl uses fehqlibs for DNS resolution (DNSSEC-aware hostname verification
against the presented certificate).  The ~conf-qlibs~ source file is patched
at build time to point at ~/usr/lib/fehqlibs~ via the
~debian-install-paths.patch~ quilt patch.

* TL;DR Runtime Documentation

** Installed binaries

All binaries land in ~/usr/bin/~.  The most commonly used:

| Binary      | Purpose                                      |
|-------------+----------------------------------------------|
| ~sslserver~ | TLS-accepting server wrapper (like tcpserver)|
| ~sslclient~ | TLS-connecting client wrapper                |
| ~sslio~     | STARTTLS relay between plaintext and TLS     |
| ~certcheck~ | Inspect / verify an X.509 certificate        |

** Typical invocation (sslserver)

#+BEGIN_SRC sh
exec /usr/bin/sslserver \
  -e -v \
  -n /etc/qmail/servercert.pem \
  0 465 \
  /var/lib/qmail/bin/qmail-smtpd 2>&1
#+END_SRC

The ~-n~ flag specifies the combined cert+key PEM file.  Environment variables
~$SSL_CLIENT_*~ are set in the child environment with peer certificate
information.

** Key environment variables (set by sslserver in child)

| Variable              | Content                                |
|-----------------------+----------------------------------------|
| ~SSL_CIPHER~          | Negotiated cipher suite                |
| ~SSL_CLIENT_DN~       | Client certificate subject DN (if any)|
| ~PROTO~               | ~SSL~                                  |
| ~TCPREMOTEIP~         | Peer IP address                        |

** Certificate requirements

~sslserver~ and ~sslclient~ expect a PEM file containing both the certificate
and private key.  The qmail package generates such a combined PEM at
~/etc/qmail/servercert.pem~.

#+BEGIN_SRC sh
# Verify a combined PEM
openssl x509 -in /etc/qmail/servercert.pem -noout -subject -dates
# Count sections (should be 2: cert + key)
grep -c 'BEGIN' /etc/qmail/servercert.pem
#+END_SRC

** Rebuilding from source

#+BEGIN_SRC sh
cd ucspi-ssl-0.13.07
dpkg-buildpackage -us -uc -b
#+END_SRC

Requires ~fehqlibs-dev~ installed first.
